properties.payload_schema:
Values crossing the boundary are `dynograph_storage::{StoredNode, StoredEdge}` and `dynograph_core::Value`, passed as owned Rust values in-process — no serialization, which is why `payload_format` is `none` rather than a wire format.

  StoredNode { graph_id: String, node_type: String, node_id: String, properties: HashMap<String, Value> }
  StoredEdge { .. from_id / to_id / edge_type / properties }

⚠️ THIS CONTRACT INHERITS ANOTHER. Those types belong to dynograph-foundation, recorded here as `ifc:req-dyno-storage-api` (designation `required` — reflow2 consumes it and does not own it). So an alternative implementation of this boundary is free to store bytes however it likes, but is NOT free to invent its own node and edge types: it must produce these. That is a real constraint on substitutability and it is inherited, not chosen.
